  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The terrorist's handbook is a work that features photographs of bridges, subways, and other infrastructural elements in New York City, within the appropriated context of a recipe book for bombs and explosives. The text, written by an unknown author and freely available on several websites, along with Schulz's photographs, serve as a palimpsest investigating individual experience within an urban physical/virtual environment dominated by fear and intolerance."--Indie Photobook Library website, viewed Nov. 15, 2013.</subfield>
  </datafield>
